          "handle": "MarioNawfal",
          "creator": "@MarioNawfal",
          "text": "🇺🇸 The U.S. Strategic Petroleum Reserve just dropped to 298.7 million barrels, it's lowest since 1983. That's before most millennials were born and when Reagan was in office. Biden drained it to fight inflation and look good at the pump. Smart short-term politics, potentially catastrophic long-term strategy. If a major supply shock hits now, America's emergency cushion is essentially a throw pillow. Source: CNBC / Writer: Oliver",
