        {
          "handle": "MarioNawfal",
          "creator": "@MarioNawfal",
          "text": "🇨🇴🇮🇱🇸🇾 Colombia today recognized Israeli sovereignty over the Golan Heights a move that puts Bogotá firmly against the international consensus that still considers it occupied Syrian territory. This is a significant pivot. Most of Latin America leans pro-Palestinian, so Colombia breaking ranks is genuinely surprising diplomatic news. Syria's new government is probably not thrilled. Israel definitely is. Watch if other Latin American nations follow. Source: cancilleria .gov .co / Writer: Oliver",
