        {
          "handle": "eliebakouch",
          "creator": "@eliebakouch",
          "text": "extremely exciting to see meta getting back into open weight models with a 30B dense first, and soon muse spark 1.2 they used knowledge distillation from muse spark, architecture wise it's similar to gemma 4 (which is llama 3 + swa (again!) + vision encoder), with scale free QK Norm (llama 4), tanh softcaping on the output layer compare to gemma 4, the model have less layer (52 vs 60), a LOT more vision layer (50 vs 27), 2x bigger swa window (2k vs 1k) and a 2x smaller attention width (4k vs 8k) one of the things that was also very exciting with the llama series was a very good tech report tha",
